## Context
Exposed by the sixth smelt (2026-11-01), page `memory/topics/commission.md`
open questions. Flagged earlier by PR #1975 (closed unmerged) as one of three
conflicts awaiting the author.

Claim A: native note `feedback_dont_idle_on_background` (Claude Code store,
read 2026-11-01, blob f7579ac3) has description line "ask the top model
(Fable) before EVERY author decision, even ones that look like the author's
by right", and the pinned night-mode line: "Not to me, it goes to Fable for
finishing. You are in night mode autonomous." The note's body was updated
2026-11-01 22:10Z to scope author-by-right calls to wait for the author, which
matches claim B; the description line still carries the unscoped wording and
is what the runtime injects.

Claim B: `rules/workflow.md` § Escalation protocol — "The author's calls by
right (scope, money, irreversible) are never branched or delegated; they
wait." A memory (or native note) cannot override a rule; the rule governs.

## Question for the author
In night mode, do calls that are the author's by right still wait for the
author, or may they go to the top advisor model first? Smelt picks no side and
proposes no rule.
